# Read by the cross-compiler (-specs=) in a build for Windows XP that names
# the C library to link (-mcrtdll=; mingw-w64-common.cmake). The default link
# line names mingw-w64's extension library (mingwex) before the C library,
# but the C library's import library calls back into it: its snprintf calls
# __ms_vsnprintf. The lines below add the two to the end of the link line as
# a group, which the linker searches until neither has more to give.

*libgcc:
+ %{mcrtdll=*:--start-group -lmingwex -l%* --end-group}
